---
description: Constraints for editing nexlayer.yaml — the Nexlayer deployment file
globs: "**/nexlayer.yaml,**/nexlayer.yml"
alwaysApply: false
---

You are editing a Nexlayer deployment file. The platform validates it before deploying, so a wrong guess costs a round trip. These constraints come from the `ship-it-nexlayer` skill — load it for anything beyond a field edit.

- Run `nexlayer_validate_yaml` after every edit and before `nexlayer_deploy`.
- App name `^[a-z][a-z0-9.-]{2,63}$`; pod name `^[a-z][a-z0-9-]{1,63}$`.
- Every image needs an explicit immutable tag. `latest` is rejected, and builds must target `linux/amd64`.
- `servicePorts` is required (except `resourceType: job`), and at least one pod needs a `path` or nothing is reachable.
- Volume sizes match `^[0-9]+(Mi|Gi)$`.
- PostgreSQL: mount at `/var/lib/postgresql/data` and set `PGDATA: /var/lib/postgresql/data/pgdata` — the data directory must be a subdirectory of the mount.
- Server-to-server URLs use `.pod` DNS (`db.pod:5432`). Anything a browser reads — `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, `VITE_*`, `REACT_APP_*`, CORS origins, OAuth callbacks — uses `<% URL %>`. `<% DOMAIN %>` is the same value without the scheme.
- No `localhost` or `127.0.0.1` in any var. Servers bind `0.0.0.0`.
- Secrets go in `secrets`, not `vars`.
